<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Renewable Energy Systems Infographic</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            background-color: #f4f4f4;
        }
        .container {
            width: 80%;
            margin: 0 auto;
            background-color: #fff;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 10px;
            box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
        }
        .header {
            text-align: center;
            padding: 20px 0;
        }
        .header h1 {
            margin: 0;
            color: #333;
        }
        .section {
            margin: 20px 0;
        }
        .section h2 {
            color: #333;
        }
        .section p {
            color: #666;
        }
        .section img {
            width: 100%;
            border-radius: 10px;
        }
        .footer {
            text-align: center;
            padding: 20px 0;
            color: #666;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="header">
            <h1>Renewable Energy Systems</h1>
        </div>
        <div class="section">
            <h2>Introduction</h2>
            <p>Renewable energy systems are sources of energy that are replenished naturally and sustainably. These include solar, wind, hydro, and geothermal energy.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="section">
            <h2>Solar Energy</h2>
            <p>Solar energy is harnessed from the sun using solar panels. It is one of the most popular forms of renewable energy due to its abundance and sustainability.</p>
            <img src="https://example.com/solar_energy.jpg" alt="Solar Energy">
        </div>
        <div class="section">
            <h2>Wind Energy</h2>
            <p>Wind energy is generated using wind turbines that convert wind kinetic energy into electrical power. It is a clean and efficient way to produce electricity.</p>
            <img src="https://example.com/wind_energy.jpg" alt="Wind Energy">
        </div>
        <div class="section">
            <h2>Hydro Energy</h2>
            <p>Hydro energy, or hydropower, is generated by harnessing the energy of flowing or falling water. It is a reliable and consistent source of renewable energy.</p>
            <img src="https://example.com/hydro_energy.jpg" alt="Hydro Energy">
        </div>
        <div class="section">
            <h2>Geothermal Energy</h2>
            <p>Geothermal energy is produced by tapping into the heat from the Earth's core. It is a stable and sustainable source of energy that can be used for heating and electricity.</p>
            <img src="https://example.com/geothermal_energy.jpg" alt="Geothermal Energy">
        </div>
        <div class="footer">
            <p>&copy; 2025 Renewable Energy Infographic</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
